CAPSTONE CHECKPOINT 3.1 - TEST RESULTS LOG
Wikipedia Retrieval Engine | Evaluation Infrastructure and Baseline Diagnosis
================================================================================

Project      : MIT Capstone - Wikipedia Retrieval Engine
Student      : Miguel Herrera
Solution     : MHERRERA_Capstone_Checkpoint_3_1_Solution.py
Corpus       : Capstone_Database/Wikipedia (~2,400 HTML articles)
Vector store : Capstone_Database/Capstone_Chroma_DB (persisted)

Configuration
  Retriever        : Hybrid (BM25 keyword + vector semantic search)
  Fusion weights   : BM25 0.5 / Vector 0.5 (min-max normalized, vector inverted)
  Top-K context    : 4 articles
  Candidate pool   : 10 per retriever side
  Answer model     : openai/gpt-5.4-mini
  Embedding model  : openai/text-embedding-3-small
  Judge / metric   : RAGAS DiscreteMetric "correctness" (pass/fail vs grading notes)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TEST RUN 1
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Test type   : Baseline RAGAS correctness evaluation - ORIGINAL questions
Date        : 2026-09-07
Start time  : ~13:06 (local)
End time    : 13:21:41 (result recorded)
Dataset     : test_variables/test_main_questions.json (100 grounded originals)
Query type  : Realistic, corpus-grounded factual questions (LLM-generated from
              article lead text; one question per distinct Wikipedia article)
Process     : For each question -> hybrid retrieve top-4 -> generate answer with
              gpt-5.4-mini -> score pass/fail with RAGAS judge against grading notes
Result      : 97/100 PASSED  (97%)
Output CSV  : ragas_experiments/experiments/distracted_hoare.csv
Failures    : 3 questions FAILED
  1. "According to the article, what authority does Article IV, Section 3,
      Clause 1 of the Constitution grant to Congress?"
      Cause: answer referenced the wrong clause (Commerce Clause) instead of the
      required point (Congress may admit new states); required fact not in context.
  2. "According to the article, who was the first first lady of the United States,
      and how many total first ladies have there been?"
      Cause: named Martha Washington correctly but could not confirm the required
      total (54); enumerated total not present in retrieved context.
  3. "How much damage did the 2011 Joplin tornado cause, and what makes it
      historically notable in terms of cost?"
      Cause: gave the $2.8 billion figure but omitted the required "costliest /
      ~$4 billion modern equivalent" point.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TEST RUN 2
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Test type   : Baseline RAGAS correctness evaluation - PARAPHRASED questions
Date        : 2026-09-07
Start time  : ~13:22 (local)
End time    : 13:37:15 (result recorded)
Dataset     : test_variables/testinputs_variant_questions.json (paraphrase rows)
Query type  : Systematic LLM paraphrases (2 per original) reusing the original's
              grading notes and sources - a rephrasing-robustness stress test
Process     : Same hybrid retrieve -> generate -> RAGAS judge pipeline as Run 1
Result      : 179/182 PASSED  (98%)
Output CSV  : ragas_experiments/experiments/amazing_rivest.csv
Failures    : 3 questions FAILED (same underlying items as Run 1)
  1. Paraphrase of the "first First Lady / total count" question - missing total.
  2. Paraphrase of the "Article IV, Section 3, Clause 1" question - wrong clause.
  3. "How many species belong to the genus Morus, and what are the three most
      common ones called..." - required specific enumeration not in context.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SIDE-BY-SIDE COMPARISON (rephrasing robustness)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Recorded    : 2026-09-07 13:37:15
  ORIGINALS    : 97/100   = 97%
  PARAPHRASES  : 179/182  = 98%
  DELTA (paraphrases - originals) : +1%
Verdict     : ROBUST to rephrasing. Paraphrase pass rate is comparable to (slightly
              above) originals, so the hybrid retriever is not brittle to wording
              changes on this test set.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EVALUATION FRAMEWORK VALIDATION (reliability check)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Test type   : Judge sensitivity to incomplete / incorrect answers
Date        : 2026-09-07
Evidence    : The RAGAS judge did not pass every answer. It correctly assigned
              FAIL to 3/100 originals (and the matching paraphrases) where the
              response missed or contradicted a required grading-notes point
              (wrong constitutional clause; missing enumerated total; omitted
              "costliest" qualifier).
Interpretation: The judge is not trivially lenient - it distinguishes complete,
              grounded answers from fluent-but-incomplete ones, which supports
              trusting the reported pass rates.
Known blind spots: judge grades answer text against notes (not against the source
              article), does not separately score retrieval hit-rate, and shares
              the gpt-5.4-mini model family with the answer generator.

